#
# Redrob OS: run the graphical first-boot wizard (initial-setup) on images that
# were written raw (Raspberry Pi 5) and therefore never saw Anaconda. The unit
# is only *enabled* here; initial-setup itself skips and disables itself when
# /etc/sysconfig/initial-setup says RUN_INITIAL_SETUP=NO, which is what the
# ISO kickstart's `firstboot --disable` writes, and once a first account exists.
# Preset numbers below 90-default-*.preset so it wins over the distro default.
enable initial-setup.service
